<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suqut al-Barghawati</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1079</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suqut al-Barghawati was a former slave of Barghawata origin who served the Hammudid rulers and became master of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a> in the mid-11th century. He ruled Ceuta as an independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> lord and resisted the advancing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>, who defeated and killed him around 1079. His son held Ceuta until the Almoravids took it in 1083.</p></div>
